From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WPS: put UUID-E in the Beacon frame in active PBC mode

wpas_wps_scan_pbc_overlap() reads a session overlap where two BSSs in
active PBC mode have UUID-E values that differ, and it takes a missing
UUID-E as one that differs. The registrar put UUID-E into the Beacon frame
only for a dual-band AP. A station that read two BSSs of one single-band
registrar from Beacon frames alone, with no Probe Response, so saw two
registrars and aborted the press.

Put UUID-E into the Beacon frame whenever the registrar is in active PBC
mode. WPS 2.0.10 Table 3 makes UUID-E in the Beacon frame mandatory for a
dual-band AP in Pushbutton mode on both radios and states no other case;
it does not forbid the attribute elsewhere. The Probe Response already holds
UUID-E in every case.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/wps/wps_registrar.c
+++ b/src/wps/wps_registrar.c
@@ -560,7 +560,7 @@ static int wps_build_sel_pbc_reg_uuid_e(
 		return 0;
 	if (reg->sel_reg_dev_password_id_override >= 0)
 		id = reg->sel_reg_dev_password_id_override;
-	if (id != DEV_PW_PUSHBUTTON || !reg->dualband)
+	if (id != DEV_PW_PUSHBUTTON)
 		return 0;
 	return wps_build_uuid_e(msg, reg->wps->uuid);
 }
